| Species | Role | Ecosystem |
|---|---|---|
| Sea otters | Control sea urchin populations | Kelp forests |
| Bees | Pollination | Basically everywhere |
| Wolves | Regulate herbivore numbers | Temperate forests |

## Food webs

A food web is a bunch of food chains linked together.
Energy flows from **producers** (plants) to **consumers** (animals) to **decomposers** (fungi, bacteria).

- Producers convert sunlight into energy through photosynthesis
- Primary consumers eat producers (herbivores)
- Secondary consumers eat primary consumers (carnivores)
- Tertiary consumers sit at the top — think eagles, sharks

> Note: energy transfer is inefficient--only about 10% of energy moves up each level.

## Biodiversity

Three types:

1. **Genetic diversity** — variation within a species
2. **Species diversity** — number of different species in an area
3. **Ecosystem diversity** — variety of ecosystems in a region

Higher biodiversity = more resilient ecosystem.
Monocultures are fragile — one disease can wipe everything out.
